  "body": "Issue #2887 asked for two things. PR #2894 (merged) did the first: the refusal of a chamfer with no picked edges on a partly bevelled edge loop. The PR left the second for later and gave no issue number. This issue holds it.\n\n## Wanted\n\nWhen a chamfer cuts only a part of an edge loop, a note names the edges that stay sharp (a point on each one). The user can then see what the operation did not cut.\n\n## Done when\n\n- A test pins the note text for a loop with one chamfered edge and one sharp edge.\n- The note is plain English and has no G-code terms.\n\nRefs #2887\n",
